+        /// ```
+        ///
+        /// `P_{k+1|k}` is solved through its Cholesky factor, never inverted. The result
+        /// holds one smoothed estimate per measurement, in measurement order; the last
+        /// one is the last filtered estimate.
+        ///
+        /// This is a query: the filter is left unchanged and can keep running afterwards.
+        /// It allocates for the forward-pass history and for the returned estimates.
+        ///
+        /// # Errors
+        /// `DimensionMismatch` if a measurement's length is not m; `InvalidInput` for a
+        /// non-finite measurement; `SingularMatrix` if a predicted covariance on the
+        /// backward path is numerically singular relative to its own scale (a state known
